-- Q889: SOC Reporting and Trust Services Criteria [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Availability (system uptime and resilience)","Processing Integrity (accurate transaction output)","Security (Common Criteria for access protection)","Privacy (personal data governance controls)"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Logical access controls that restrict access to information assets based on roles fall under the Security (Common Criteria) category per the AICPA Trust Services Framework. Security controls protect against unauthorized access and form the foundation of the framework.
Wrong (A): Availability addresses system uptime and usability, not access restriction to information assets.
Wrong (B): Processing Integrity addresses completeness and accuracy of system processing, not logical access controls.
Wrong (D): Privacy addresses personal information governance, not role-based access controls over information assets generally.$EXPL$
