-- Q3432: IT Infrastructure and Architecture [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Reduced hardware costs due to fewer network components required","Simplified troubleshooting from a single unified broadcast domain","Faster data transfer speeds between all connected network devices","Unrestricted lateral movement for any compromised device on the network"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): In a flat network with no segmentation, any compromised device has unrestricted lateral movement across the entire broadcast domain, violating NIST SP 800-53 SC-7 (Boundary Protection). Malware or an attacker on one workstation can directly reach financial servers and databases.
Wrong (A): Reduced hardware costs are a potential benefit, not a risk, of flat network design.
Wrong (B): Simplified troubleshooting is a potential operational advantage, not a security risk.
Wrong (C): Faster transfer speeds are a performance characteristic, not a risk; the primary concern is the lack of internal barriers to contain breaches.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3432;

