-- Q3451: IT Infrastructure and Architecture [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Compliance risk from running multiple applications on shared hardware","Performance risk from insufficient application workload on the server","Legal risk from consolidating disparate business services together","Single point of failure risk where one hardware failure disrupts everything"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Per NIST SP 800-34 Rev. 1 (Contingency Planning Guide), Section 3.4, organizations must identify and mitigate single points of failure. A single server hosting accounting, email, and file services creates concentrated availability risk because any hardware failure disables all services simultaneously.
Wrong (A): Running multiple applications on shared hardware is common and not inherently a compliance risk.
Wrong (B): Insufficient workload is not a recognized risk category; the concern is excessive concentration, not underutilization.
Wrong (C): Consolidating services does not create a legal risk; the risk is operational availability, not legal liability.$EXPL$
