-- Q3463: IT Infrastructure and Architecture [hard/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Strangler fig pattern with an anti-corruption translation layer","Complete cloud migration replacing all legacy systems at once","Monolithic deployment consolidating everything into one application","Serverless computing eliminating all infrastructure management overhead"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Per COBIT 2019 BAI03 (Managed Solutions Identification and Build), the strangler fig pattern gradually replaces legacy functionality with modern services while an anti-corruption layer translates between old and new interfaces. This enables incremental modernization without high-risk big-bang migration.
Wrong (B): Complete cloud migration describes a full cutover, not the incremental pattern with a translation layer described in the scenario.
Wrong (C): Monolithic deployment consolidates all functionality into a single application, which is the opposite of the microservices approach described.
Wrong (D): Serverless computing is a hosting model, not an architectural integration pattern for connecting legacy and modern systems.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3463;

