-- Q3474: ERP and Accounting Information Systems [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Role-based access controls separating vendor, invoice, and payment functions","Strong password requirements for the accounts payable clerk''s login","CAPTCHA verification on the vendor creation form to prevent automation","Encryption of the entire accounts payable database at rest"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Role-based access controls (RBAC) enforce segregation of duties by restricting users to defined roles with non-overlapping permissions per NIST SP 800-53 AC-5 (Separation of Duties). Separating vendor creation, invoice entry, and payment approval prevents one individual from executing end-to-end fraud.
